        {
          "id": 1247123732,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The resources usually get unpacked during application startup. This adds delay especially on older hardware. \n\nIn General I agree about the usage, but it is somewhat expected from an open source project to have that as a File, is it not?\n\nPersonally I only care about the startup delay and just wanted to voice the viewpoint. I can live with either solution",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-01-20T10:21:55.590Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-01-20T10:21:55.590Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 200432605,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2023-01-20T12:08:27.639Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 9541,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 1247148682,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I think the delay is negligible. If by unpacked you mean decompression I assume that only happens when opening the About Dialog. Small binary size is a worthwhile goal in general but IMO this is an acceptable compromise.\n\n> In General I agree about the usage, but it is somewhat expected from an open source project to have that as a File, is it not?\n\nI don't know about expected but it is common. But we can still provide the AUTHORS file (with tasks and pretty formatting maybe) if we want. That is documentation and it should go in $docdir.\n\nCurrently we ship AUTHORS-SHORT to $datadir. IMO that doesn't fulfill the goal of providing a documentation file with a list of contributors for distribution that you were referring to (except through the GUI of course).",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2023-01-20T10:36:51.543Z",
          "updated_at": "2023-01-20T10:36:51.543Z",
